# records of bce2ce3daf8df9a0
# `if ((type as TypeReference).node)`: the type behind the cast requires the field, a store by name appends it, most objects are without it. The look at the slot parts three ways:
# filled: the typed run . EMPTY, and the object's own byte and the guard of the class say that nothing stands above and nothing lies outside the slots: the read is undefined, the branch folds, the side is three looks and a jump . else closed.
# f1 = use, f2 = flagsOf. A field of the birth (`flags`) gets no such side: its slot is never empty, and what the side would bring is met by what the typed run brings.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[filled]]: boolean @Boolean = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="part"
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[filled]] -> taken {{*}}, notTaken [[empty]]()
# CHECK: [[empty]]():
# CHECK-NEXT: = HasNoFieldOutsideSlot
# CHECK: = HasLayoutPrototype
# CHECK: = AreMembersUnchanged {{*}}key="part"
# RUN(BIRTH): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# BIRTH-LABEL: code f2:Body
# BIRTH-NOT: = HasNoFieldOutsideSlot
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: none
# ANSWERS: has 3
# ANSWERS: has 5
# ANSWERS: has 3

